   combined_replication.docx document, and the research notes in this
   repository.

3. ORIGINAL PAPER, DATASETS, AND THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL - NOT covered by
   either license above. See Section C below.

If a single file is unclear in scope (e.g. a file combining code and
documentation), the more permissive of the two licenses applies.

NOTE ON A LICENSE CHANGE: earlier versions of this repository carried
a single-file LICENSE under Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-
NoDerivatives 4.0 (CC BY-NC-ND 4.0). That text contradicted the MIT
(code) and CC BY 4.0 (documentation) terms stated in README.md and
CITATION.cff. It has been replaced by the dual license in this file,
which is what the README and CITATION.cff already described. Copies of
the repository obtained before this change were distributed under the
earlier terms.

